# Force LF line endings for files consumed by Unix shells.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows corrupts shebangs at
# checkout: `#!/bin/bash\r\n` makes execve(2) look up an interpreter
# literally named `bash\r`, fails with ENOENT, and the SSH channel is
# closed before any tar byte reaches the server. See the 2026-05-15
# incident: helper deployed in CRLF, mirror upload aborted 1 s in with
# "Socket is closed".
*.sh text eol=lf
